{"name":"Balsam Brown","hex":"#cba874","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"balsam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet-smelling oil or resin derived from various plants.","A plant or tree yielding such substance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat or anoint with balsam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balsam"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balsam","blocks":[{"text":"Balsam is the resinous exudate which forms on certain kinds of trees and shrubs, particularly species belonging to genera such as Myroxylon, Abies, Copaifera, Styrax, and Populus. They may occur naturally as resinous exudates following injury to bark or wood tissues. Balsam owes its name to the biblical Balm of Gilead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG/330px-Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balsam","wikidata":"Q1776037"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg/500px-Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten